      "folder": "Phase_5_Commissioning_L1_L5_RIBA_5_6\\PM-27_Cx_L3_Static_BSRIA_Flush_LOTO",
      "keyFacts": [
        "Milestone: M6260 Level 3 Static & Energization Gate (2029-08-20)",
        "HV Safety: Senior Authorized Person (SAP) + written LOTO + Sanction-for-Test",
        "Electrical Static: 0.1 Hz VLF Hi-Pot cable test, Megger IR, relay injection",
        "Mechanical Static: BSRIA BG 29 pre-commission flush + CHW pressure tests",
        "Prerequisite: White -> Green Tag sign-off by CxA before closing main breaker"
      ],
      "readme": "# PM-27: Cx Level 3: Pre-Functional Static, BSRIA Flush & LOTO\n\n- **Phase**: `Phase 5: Commissioning L1-L5 & Integrated Testing (RIBA 5-6)`\n- **RIBA Stage**: `RIBA Stage 5`\n- **P6 Milestone Gate**: `M6260 (2029-08-20)`\n- **WBS Scope**: `WBS 6.2-L3`\n- **Governing Standards**: BSRIA BG 29 Pre-Commission Cleaning, HV/LV Safe Switching LOTO\n- **Focus Areas**: SAP LOTO Permit Book, Megger / VLF Hi-Pot, Relay Injection, CHW Chemical Flush, Pressure / Leakage Certs\n\n## Module Overview\nVerify Megger/hi-pot insulation, relay secondary injection, BSRIA chilled-water flushing, and strict LOTO energisation permits.\n\n## Ordered Flashcard Documents (`Doc 1` -> `Doc 4`)\n\n| Doc | Category | Title | Exact Local File | Companion / Notes |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Doc 1 | Standard | BSRIA BG 29 Pre-Commission Cleaning of Pipework & HV Safe Switching Rules | `PM27_Doc1_Standard_BSRIA_BG_29_Pre_Commission_Cleaning_Rev.004.docx` | BSRIA BG 29 / ESBN Safety |\n| Doc 2 | Deliverable | Authorized HV/LV Lockout-Tagout (LOTO) Control Book & Sanction-for-Test | `PM27_Doc2_Deliverable_Authorized_HV_LV_Lockout_Tagout_Rev.004.docx` | SAP / Authorized Person Book |\n| Doc 3 | Template | Level 3 Electrical Static Checksheets (Megger, VLF Hi-Pot & Relay Injection) | `PM27_Doc3_Template_Level_3_Electrical_Static_Rev.004.xlsx` | L3 Electrical Static Pack |\n| Doc 4 | Audit | BSRIA Closed-Loop Chilled-Water Chemical Flushing & Leakage Certificates | `PM27_Doc4_Audit_BSRIA_Closed_Loop_Chilled_Water_Rev.004.xlsx` | BSRIA BG 29 / Duct Leakage |\n\n## Study Takeaway (`Why Each Document Matters`)\n- **Doc 1 (Standard)**: Prevent condenser fouling and arc-flash hazards through strict static qualification.\n- **Doc 2 (Deliverable)**: Enforce Safe System of Work and Authorised Person isolation across live zones.\n- **Doc 3 (Template)**: Validate busbar torque thermography marks, CT polarity, and relay trip curves.\n- **Doc 4 (Audit)**: Confirm turbidity, iron <5 ppm, biocide dosing, and pressurized pipe integrity.\n",
