      "readme": "# PM-30: Dual EN 50600 Class 3 & Uptime TCCF Constructed Audit\n\n- **Phase**: `Phase 5: Commissioning L1-L5 & Integrated Testing (RIBA 5-6)`\n- **RIBA Stage**: `RIBA Stage 6`\n- **P6 Milestone Gate**: `A7040 / M7060`\n- **WBS Scope**: `WBS 7.0-COD`\n- **Governing Standards**: Uptime Institute TCCF Rulebook, I.S. EN 50600-2-x Class 3 Audit\n- **Focus Areas**: Path A vs. Path B Isolation, SPOF Pre-Audit Sheet, Assessor Observations, Concurrent Maint. Proof, Constructed Certificates\n\n## Module Overview\nScript simultaneous path-isolation concurrent maintainability demonstrations for independent on-site certifying assessors.\n\n## Ordered Flashcard Documents (`Doc 1` -> `Doc 4`)\n\n| Doc | Category | Title | Exact Local File | Companion / Notes |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Doc 1 | Standard | Uptime Institute Tier Standard Topology (TCCF) & I.S. EN 50600 Class 3 Rules | `PM30_Doc1_Standard_Uptime_Institute_Tier_Standard_Rev.004.docx` | Uptime TCCF / EN 50600 |\n| Doc 2 | Deliverable | On-Site Assessor Concurrent Maintainability Isolation Demonstration Pack | `PM30_Doc2_Deliverable_On_Site_Assessor_Concurrent_Rev.004.docx` | Path A vs. Path B Proofs |\n| Doc 3 | Template | Pre-Audit Single-Point-of-Failure (SPOF) Electrical & Cooling Walkdown Sheet | `PM30_Doc3_Template_Pre_Audit_Single_Point_of_Failure_Rev.004.xlsx` | SPOF Elimination Check |\n| Doc 4 | Audit | Assessor Observations Remediation Dossier & Constructed Certificate File | `PM30_Doc4_Audit_Assessor_Observations_Remediation_Rev.004.docx` | Certification Sign-Off Vault |\n\n## Study Takeaway (`Why Each Document Matters`)\n- **Doc 1 (Standard)**: Satisfy both Uptime Institute assessors and European EN 50600 third-party auditors.\n- **Doc 2 (Deliverable)**: Prove every switchgear, transformer, UPS, and chiller header isolates with zero outage.\n- **Doc 3 (Template)**: Eliminate shared control PLC power supplies, manual valve bypasses, or control loops.\n- **Doc 4 (Audit)**: Close minor witness punch items and secure final bankable facility certificates.\n",
